### `Compression — opt-in tool-result summarization`

The `--compress` flag enables tool-result compression:

- **Tool-result compression**: tool output > threshold chars is summarized by flash model
- **Fail-open**: empty or error summaries → original content sent upstream (no quality loss)
- **Content-hash cache** + singleflight dedup: same content compressed only once
- **Flash model** (`deepseek-v4-flash`) used for summarization

| Aspect | Detail |
| ------- | ------ |
| Flag | `--compress` (CLI), `CompressEnabled bool` |
| Default | `false` (off) — must be explicitly enabled |
| Threshold | `toolResultMaxLen` (controlling when tool output gets compressed) |
| Strategy | Tool-result message compression only |
| Cache | Content-hash keyed, singleflight dedup, semaphore-bounded concurrency |
| Fail-open | On any error (timeout, rejection, empty summary), original body returned unchanged |

#### Debugging compression from logs

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| `grep "compress"` returns no matches in gateway JSONL logs | Escaped JSON strings defeat literal grep | Parse with `python3 -c "import json,sys; [print(l.strip()) for l in sys.stdin if 'compress' in l.lower()]"` — use JSONL-aware parsing, not raw grep |
| `compress: flash model returned empty summary (content N chars)` warning | Flash model occasionally fails to produce a summary for certain content | Expected — compression is fail-open so original content is sent upstream; no quality degradation. Tune if >20% failure rate. The HTTP client timeout for flash calls is 8s (fail-fast, don't block the user-visible turn). |
| Compression saves no tokens (cache hits all misses) | Content-hash cache not warmed, or content is already under compression threshold | Expected for first request with unique content; significant savings appear on multi-turn sessions with repeated tool results |
| Many `compress: skipping verbatim tool result` DEBUG lines | Every tool result (file reads, searches, diffs) triggered a debug log when `--log-level debug`; this log has been removed | The `compress: tool_results` INFO log reports actual compressions; per-tool skip logging is unnecessary noise |

#### Performance: inline auxiliary API calls must fail fast

Auxiliary API calls (compression, vision description) that run synchronously on
the request-serving goroutine must use short timeouts so failures don't add
latency to the user-visible turn:

- HTTP client timeout ≤ 8s for flash/auxiliary summarizer calls
- Fast-scan early-return before building expensive data structures: if a cheap
  heuristic says no work is needed (e.g. all tool messages are verbatim file
  reads), return immediately before allocating maps or marshaling payloads
- Content-hash cache + singleflight before any outbound call (already done)

